# API Auth Data Rules

- Treat auth/session, role permissions, and student/parent data as high-risk areas.
- Validate API inputs at the boundary. Prefer existing schema validation; otherwise use Zod.
- Never expose secrets, tokens, credentials, or internal error details to clients.
- Check permissions close to the data access point, not only in UI.
- For admin CMS, define allowed roles explicitly.
- Do not change migrations, schema, or persisted data shape without explicit approval.
- For Firebase/Supabase/NextAuth, follow existing project patterns before adding custom auth logic.
- For MongoDB, validate object IDs and query filters before database calls.
